ss_url`, `canonicalize_json`, `list_scan_rules`\nLibrary  | `import { Warden } from \"@aimarket/warden\"`\nGlama / Docker (stdio)  | `Dockerfile`, `glama.json`\nOfficial MCP Registry  | `server.json` → `io.github.alexar76/warden`\nSmithery  | `smithery.yaml`\n\nAn MCP server tells your agent what its tools do. The agent believes it — that sentence is the attack surface. A tool description is prompt text delivered by a third party straight into your model's context, and a schema field named `api_key` is a request for your secrets phrased as an API.\n\nWARDEN vets a server before any of its tools reach the model, and returns a verdict you can record: allow/block, a 0..1 score, the findings that produced it, a per-tool partition, and the exact rule table that was in force.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nwarden MCP server · io.github.alexar76 · ProtocolProbe (https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/io.github.alexar76/warden)\nciteturn3search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago;     code --add-mcp '{\"name\":\"warden\",\"type\":\"stdio\",\"command\":\"npx\",\"args\":[\"-y\",\"@aimarket/warden@0.22.2\"]}' ... Repository github.com/alexar76/warden  | Opens publicly  | matches  | api.github.com · 2026-10-31\n\nWhat it is\n\n## How do I add it to my client?\n\nConfig from the registry entry\n\n### From the npm package @aimarket/warden\n\nAdd to Cursor An install link in the format Cursor documents, holding the Cursor config below. The command runs the publisher’s code on your machine.\n\nClaude Desktop · claude_desktop_config.json (Settings → Developer → Edit Config)\n    \n    {\n      \"mcpServers\": {\n        \"warden\": {\n          \"command\": \"npx\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"-y\",\n            \"@aimarket/warden@0.22.2\"\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    }\n\nCursor · .cursor/mcp.json in a project, or ~/.cursor/mcp.json\n    \n    {\n      \"mcpServers\": {\n        \"warden\": {\n          \"comm